    <Label Name="Title" Style="GalleryTitle" Text="Inscribed Circle" Pin="TopRight" OffsetX="16" OffsetY="36.25" WrapWidth="400" Backdrop="true" />
    <Label Name="Description" Style="GalleryText" Text="Every triangle has exactly one circle that touches all three sides: its incircle.\n\nThe green lines are the angle bisectors. They always meet in a single point, the incenter (gray) — the center of the incircle. A perpendicular from the incenter to a side gives the green point where the circle touches.\n\nDrag the yellow vertices: the circle always fits." Pin="TopRight" OffsetX="16" OffsetY="84.25" WrapWidth="400" Backdrop="true" />
